  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Plage de la Douane is one of the small beaches and coves that extend Escalet beach towards Cap Taillat, on Ramatuelle's coastal path. It takes its name from the customs officers' house that still stands right by the water, built under Napoleon I and recently restored. The white sand here is some of the finest on the Côte d'Azur, with a direct view of Cap Taillat — Ramatuelle's tourist office ranks it among the town's most beautiful beaches.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>All of Ramatuelle's beaches — Pampelonne, Bonne Terrasse, Escalet and the coves beyond, including la Douane — welcome dogs on leash year-round, with no set hours, according to the "Dog friendly" leaflet published by Ramatuelle's tourist office. Swimming remains forbidden in the swimming-only zones (ZRUB), signposted at the lifeguard posts. Plage de la Douane itself is unsupervised and can only be reached on foot, via the coastal path.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: start from the Escalet car park (the furthest right one) and take the path to the right — Plage de la Douane is about a 10-minute walk away, well before Cap Taillat.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed at Plage de la Douane?</h3>
      <p>Yes, on leash, year-round, with no set hours — as on every beach in Ramatuelle.</p>
      <h3>Is there a water point on site?</h3>
      <p>No, no water point is reported along the way — remember to bring water for your dog.</p>
      <h3>How do you reach Plage de la Douane?</h3>
      <p>On foot only, via the coastal path, from the Escalet car park (about 10 minutes) or from Pampelonne/Bonne Terrasse.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The path continues towards <a href="/en/fiche-plage-cap-taillat">Cap Taillat</a>, on the border with La Croix-Valmer. For a more accessible, better-equipped beach, head to <a href="/en/fiche-pampelonne">Pampelonne Beach</a> or <a href="/en/fiche-bonne-terrasse">Bonne Terrasse Beach</a>. For a family-friendly beach with rinse showers, head to <a href="/en/fiche-escalet">Escalet Beach</a>, the starting point of the trail.</p>
    </div>

